{"parentUuid":"d317bd92-cd06-4968-94c2-8cc0a90ca1d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch68NJNkiXb5z1eJb5tQd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both 281 findings are resolved, and #483 is pushed as 734fd846. The second one, the depth-zero collapse of a named callback type, needed no code fix.\n\nThe worker found it doesn't reproduce on the current code. The factory callback's named props type is already resolved at depth zero, so its own members stay listed. The reviewer saw #483's older copy of the factory code, which the merge 39646670 replaced. The worker added regression tests to #480, and I merged them into #483:\n- 201 own members stay listed under `dependencies` and `all`, for both a named and an inline annotation.\n- An extended 201-member source still collapses while the interface's own members stay listed.\n\nThose tests pass on both branches (19 in `factory_props`), and I wrote the resolution note to say plainly that no source change was needed. The worker hasn't run a full nextest or `/code-review`. I haven't re-run the workspace suite since the last merge. It passed (1640 tests) before the tests-only merge.\n\n**State:** #480 and #483 have no open findings. Merge order is #480, then #483.\n\n**On the michi note:** I'm not acting on it. Caliper's canonical JSON stays the source of truth, and TOON isn't changing in this work. When michi 0.10 ships, it needs a comparison on the same fixtures, as they said."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_read_input_tokens":695190,"output_tokens":432,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":421,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_to