{"parentUuid":"f67ba1af-cce0-4503-848b-0745883a0874","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch691JqKK7F9LaNyo7Qzs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":171,"cache_read_input_tokens":707270,"output_tokens":3307,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1389},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":171,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3307,"cache_read_input_tokens":707270,"cache_creation_input_tokens":171,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":171},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":12233,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"9c1d0618-3956-4c5d-bdaa-e8dda261fcf8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch691JXxGWZfjwCGxnYBu","requestRef":"c0aa1df5-ef87-4ae5-9f90-b6d26808a514","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e40d800d-1e59-4c59-ba24-6dbab8163771","timestamp":"2026-11-16T06:32:30.454Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf6-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"e40d800d-1e59-4c59-ba24-6dbab8163771","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch691JqKK7F9LaNyo7Qzs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B4N4YcX7CirRVtwH9ddhL7","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Rewrite changesets for users before the release","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Rewrite the pending changesets so they read as a user-facing changelog, per the convention in AGENTS.md (section 'Writing and commits': read it fully), before the next release. Start from `origin/main` (`git fetch origin` first; if blocked use existing refs), local branch `docs/user-focused-changesets`; commit locally; I push and open the PR. Read /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md, then every file in `.changeset/` (collapse-large-sources-by-default, checker-bounds-converted-type-size, extract-heap-budget, skip-converting-collapsed-layer-props, jsx-evidence-in-extractor, structural-parity-utility-and-generics, factory-own-props, relevance-output, scheduler-priority-and-cancel, scheduler-addon-wiring) and a couple of older released entries in CHANGELOG.md files for tone (`git log -p --stat -- '**/CHANGELOG.md' | head`). The convention: one file per consumer-visible topic with a front matter line per affected package; open with a BOLD lead-in naming the change as the user sees it, then one line on its value; then short bullets in this order: why it matters, how to adopt it (commands/config/migration), limits they will hit; group longer entries under bold labels (**Upgrading**, **Scripting**); no `#` headings; a breaking change in its own paragraph starting `**Breaking:**` (old behavior, new behavior, what to do) and required user steps in a paragraph starting `**Action:**`, never inside a bullet; one idea per bullet; leave out internals (struct fields, cache schema numbers, crate-internal types, ADR numbers) unless library users must know; never hard-wrap Markdown (one line per paragraph); succinct, no banned words (see docs/adr/README.md). Facts you may rely on (verify against code/docs when unsure, do not invent): (1) collapse by default: `collapseInheritedProps` default 'dependencies' in the Storybook addon (was 'none'), a source of more than 200 props (ambient/DOM/ARIA/style sources more than 30) becomes one inheritance layer of names; own and notable props stay listed; Chakra median props per component 845 -> 139, Button Controls ~1141 -> ~146; this is a BREAKING change for the addon's default output: `Action:` set 'none' to keep every inherited prop; also: a prop the project itself declares next to React's types (`ComponentProps<'div'> & { className: 'mine' }`) stays listed, a collapsed layer never repeats a listed prop, and a source behind an unresolved `Omit` key set is not collapsed (PR 485). (2) memory: a checker extract of Chakra's own source took 42 GB on 0.11.0; now a type over 18,724 nodes is cut to its name and extraction stops asking the checker past a heap budget (60% of available memory, at most 8 GiB, cgroup-aware, including cgroup v1 comounted mounts), with a SEMANTIC_BACKEND warning. (3) the checker skips converting props held in collapsed layers (faster, memory down, output unchanged). (4) schema version 8: collapsed layers gain `used` (ambient members consumers pass or bodies read); consumers must read version 8 (Vite plugin, Storybook addon, scripts, oracle already do). (5) factory-built components (Chakra `chakra('div', {variants})`, `createLeafComponent`) gain own props: variant keys, render function annotation (props types, destructuring defaults, discriminated unions), only for proven render functions; Spectrum missing props 2216 -> 359, Chakra 13 -> 11. (6) structural answer: `ReactElement`/`JSX.Element` stay named; structural `Partial/Required/Pick/Omit` are NOT expanded (the checker answers them), type parameters and handler aliases as the existing changeset says; read the current file and keep only what is true on main (the expansion bullets were deleted by PR 475's final change). (7) on-demand checker scheduling: the story shown is answered first, neighbours next, warm-up last; navigation cancels queued neighbour work; a queued request waits at most a bounded number of picks. (8) jsx-evidence: crate-internal; library users only: `ComponentMapping::new` / `SourceData::default()` — keep as a short library-users note or fold into relevance-output. Add a NEW changeset for PR 485 (item 1's last sentence) and fold facts into the right topic if one already covers it. Fix stale numbers (parse cache version is irrelevant to users: drop it). Packages: keep the existing front-matter package lines unless wrong; run `just semver` to confirm the bump levels the project's tooling expects and fix if it complains (the 0.x minor bump covers breaking). Gates: `just lint doc-check machete typos`, `just semver` (report exit codes). Also check docs/ for a place that documents the addon default (`collapseInheritedProps` default in docs and package README) and fix any statement that still says 'none' by default (grep -rn \"collapseInheritedProps\" docs packages README.md). Cap 40 tool calls. Final message at most 50 words: branch, SHA, exit codes, which changesets were rewritten."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":171,"cache_read_input_tokens":707270,"output_tokens":3307,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1389},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":171,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3307,"cache_read_input_tokens":707270,"cache_creation_input_tokens":171,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":171}