{"parentUuid":"79952ce0-ef07-4aac-92a5-4f51f2589a10","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch69DwBgHZ5xgh1syrhW8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019Ys9ocEHQ5ykjKiw9kCmKy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 1,50p docs/storybook-parity.md | cut -c1-240"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":923,"cache_read_input_tokens":725211,"output_tokens":143,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":923,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":143,"cache_read_input_tokens":725211,"cache_creation_input_tokens":923,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":923},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019Ys9ocEHQ5ykjKiw9kCmKy":{"command":"sed -n 1,50p docs/storybook-parity.md | cut -c1-240"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3455c280-cd2e-4079-95bf-76919eec302f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch69DvqqeJkZQ58f4vQgP","requestRef":"5a643cae-a427-4a05-b49d-35202dea5c1b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"40407497-25c6-4fda-b669-4cdbe5e96fbe","timestamp":"2026-11-16T06:35:10.161Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf6-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"79952ce0-ef07-4aac-92a5-4f51f2589a10","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"08d8dfa9-12ad-4625-aa58-11e91c631e1d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RnXWXyYreXBdDf91ECchpy","type":"tool_result","content":"# Status\n\n**Updated:** 2026-11-12\n\nCore extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are fully tested. Config file loading, watch mode (including rebuilds on config changes and polling with `ensure_fresh`), plugin architecture, TOON token-optimized o\n\n**Types from other packages.** Imports resolve to any file under a source directory, `.d.ts` included, so a monorepo whose packages are all source directories resolves across them. By default the declarations those names point to are loaded\n\n## Numbers\n\n- Rust tests (`cargo nextest` across the workspace, plus the NAPI binding tests) and vitest (unit with a mocked binding, integration against the real native binding), all green in CI\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` clean with `unsafe_code = \"deny\"` enforced workspace-wide\n- 20 real-world fixture libraries validated against `react-docgen-typescript` (shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda, react-final-form, react-resi\n- **Recall** against `react-docgen-typescript` with dependencies installed and loaded: the share of RDT's reference components and props that Caliper also reports, not a measure of correctness (the checker judges that; on the props both lis\n- **Precision** per detection rule (`docs/precision.md`, 2026-10-21): 1 component that isn't one in 154 sampled, `functionDeclaration` 96% and every other rule 100%. 25 samples per rule can't yet establish the 95% gate.\n- **Speed, with the checker (the default):** `extract` of 938 Chakra UI and MUI wrappers takes 6.05 s and about 970 MiB, 787 Chakra wrappers alone 5.4 s and 770 MiB, 2,814 components 15.4 s and 1,053 MiB (`docs/gate-measurements.md`, 2026-1\n- **Speed, structural resolver (`--no-checker`)** on five pinned public corpora (`docs/performance.md`, 2026-10-22): 34 to 81 ms wall time and 66 to 153 MB peak RSS for 41 to 490 kLOC, 17 to 39 times faster than `react-docgen-typescript` on\n\n## Features and improvements\n\n- **`htmlAttributes` defaults to `full`** — every attribute `@types/react` declares is listed, `ref` for `forwardRef` and `ComponentProps<\"div\">` props; `curated` is an opt-in compact mode. Costs against the old default: wall time +9 to +31\n- **Testing Stack** — `cargo-nextest` process runner, `rstest` parameterized spec tables, `insta` snapshots, and `trycmd` executable Markdown CLI specs.\n- **TOON output format** (`--format toon` / `toon.rs`) — Token-optimized format for LLM agents, cutting context window token usage by ~65-75%.\n- **JSON schema export** (`caliper-docgen schema`) — Machine-readable Draft-07 JSON Schema export for component metadata validation.\n- **Atomic & Bounded DTS cache** (`cache.rs`) — Atomic temp-file swap writes, dirty flag tracking, and 5,000 entry eviction cap. Keyed by content hash, and discarded whenever the build that wrote it differs.\n- **Lazy sessions** (ADR 0016) — `WatchSession::lazy` parses and indexes every file and resolves a component when a request names it; the Storybook addon uses it by default (NAPI `lazy`, off by default). Each answer equals the batch extract\n- **Dependency declarations loaded by default** (ADR 0010) — a prop typed by an installed package resolves; `--no-load-dependencies` turns it off.\n- **Strict Safe Rust** — `unsafe_code = \"deny\"` via `[workspace.lints]`, active across all five crates — none currently use `unsafe`, including the NAPI FFI boundary (napi-rs's `#[napi]` macros generate the glue without user-visible `unsafe\n\n## Known gaps of the structural resolver (the fallback, and `--no-checker`)\n\nSee the \"Known gaps summary\" table in `rdt-coverage.md` for the full, maintained list. The short version: conditional types that need inference (`infer`, an unbound generic), mapped types over an unbound generic, and a couple of `@emotion/s\n\n**The TypeScript checker is the default** (ADR 0026, S8 done 2026-11-12). `extract`, `check` and `inspect` merge the built-in checker's answer (the `tsrs` crates, the only checker since trail 369 slice 4 removed `--tsc-path`) over the struc\n\n## Experiments that didn't pan out\n\n**Confidence routing (2026-10-25).** The idea: score each component's risk of wrong or missing props from Caliper's own output, and ask the TypeScript 7.1 checker only about the risky ones. Measured against the checker on 518,268 shared pro\n\n## Where to look next\n\n- **Open gaps** → `edge-cases.md` — the gaps still open. Add one when you find a gap you aren't fixing now; delete it when you fix it.\n- **Where Caliper's types differ from RDT and the checker, and what that costs** → `rdt-differences.md`.\n- **What broke and why, historically** → `rdt-coverage.md` — every bug found during real-library validation, root cause, and the fix. Keep this updated; it's the project's memory.\n- **Why a hard-to-reverse decision was made** → `docs/adr/` — OXC over the TypeScript compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack encoding, panic containment, the TypeScript 7 semantic backend. Write a new one when you make a \n- **How the pipeline fits together** → `ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `docs/architecture/` for per-subsystem invariants and known gaps (moved from `.claude/semantic-model/` so every coding agent can read it, not just Claude Code — `AGENTS.md` is no\n- **Setup, testing, code style, commit conventions** → `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n- **Migrating from react-docgen-typescript** → `MIGRATING.md`","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8671d1c1-1d83-4458-9b0a-a5664667dd45","timestamp":"2026-11-16T06:35:10.654Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Status\n\n**Updated:** 2026-11-12\n\nCore extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are fully tested. Config file loading, watch mode (including rebuilds on config changes and polling with `ensure_fresh`), plugin architecture, TOON token-optimized o\n\n**Types from other packages.** Imports resolve to any file under a source directory, `.d.ts` included, so a monorepo whose packages are all source directories resolves across them. By default the declarations those names point to are loaded\n\n## Numbers\n\n- Rust tests (`cargo nextest` across the workspace, plus the NAPI binding tests) and vitest (unit with a mocked binding, integration against the real native binding), all green in CI\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` clean with `unsafe_code = \"deny\"` enforced workspace-wide\n- 20 real-world fixture libraries validated against `react-docgen-typescript` (shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda, react-final-form, react-resi\n- **Recall** against `react-docgen-typescript` with dependencies installed and loaded: the share of RDT's reference components and props that Caliper also reports, not a measure of correctness (the checker judges that; on the props both lis\n- **Precision** per detection rule (`docs/precision.md`, 2026-10-21): 1 component that isn't one in 154 sampled, `functionDeclaration` 96% and every other rule 100%. 25 samples per rule can't yet establish the 95% gate.\n- **Speed, with the checker (the default):** `extract` of 938 Chakra UI and MUI wrappers takes 6.05 s and about 970 MiB, 787 Chakra wrappers alone 5.4 s and 770 MiB, 2,814 components 15.4 s and 1,053 MiB (`docs/gate-measurements.md`, 2026-1\n- **Speed, structural resolver (`--no-checker`)** on five pinned public corpora (`docs/performance.md`, 2026-10-22): 34 to 81 ms wall time and 66 to 153 MB peak RSS for 41 to 490 kLOC, 17 to 39 times faster than `react-docgen-typescript` on\n\n## Features and improvements\n\n- **`htmlAttributes` defaults to `full`** — every attribute `@types/react` declares is listed, `ref` for `forwardRef` and `ComponentProps<\"div\">` props; `curated` is an opt-in compact mode. Costs against the old default: wall time +9 to +31\n- **Testing Stack** — `cargo-nextest` process runner, `rstest` parameterized spec tables, `insta` snapshots, and `trycmd` executable Markdown CLI specs.\n- **TOON output format** (`--format toon` / `toon.rs`) — Token-optimized format for LLM agents, cutting context window token usage by ~65-75%.\n- **JSON schema export** (`caliper-docgen schema`) — Machine-readable Draft-07 JSON Schema export for component metadata validation.\n- **Atomic & Bounded DTS cache** (`cache.rs`) — Atomic temp-file swap writes, dirty flag tracking, and 5,000 entry eviction cap. Keyed by content hash, and discarded whenever the build that wrote it differs.\n- **Lazy sessions** (ADR 0016) — `WatchSession::lazy` parses and indexes every file and resolves a component when a request names it; the Storybook addon uses it by default (NAPI `lazy`, off by default). Each answer equals the batch extract\n- **Dependency declarations loaded by default** (ADR 0010) — a prop typed by an installed package resolves; `--no-load-dependencies` turns it off.\n- **Strict Safe Rust** — `unsafe_code = \"deny\"` via `[workspace.lints]`, active across all five crates — none currently use `unsafe`, including the NAPI FFI boundary (napi-rs's `#[napi]` macros generate the glue without user-visible `unsafe\n\n## Known gaps of the structural resolver (the fallback, and `--no-checker`)\n\nSee the \"Known gaps summary\" table in `rdt-coverage.md` for the full, maintained list. The short version: conditional types that need inference (`infer`, an unbound generic), mapped types over an unbound generic, and a couple of `@emotion/s\n\n**The TypeScript checker is the default** (ADR 0026, S8 done 2026-11-12). `extract`, `check` and `inspect` merge the built-in checker's answer (the `tsrs` crates, the only checker since trail 369 slice 4 removed `--tsc-path`) over the struc\n\n## Experiments that didn't pan out\n\n**Confidence routing (2026-10-25).** The idea: score each component's risk of wrong or missing props from Caliper's own output, and ask the TypeScript 7.1 checker only about the risky ones. Measured against the checker on 518,268 shared pro\n\n## Where to look next\n\n- **Open gaps** → `edge-cases.md` — the gaps still open. Add one when you find a gap you aren't fixing now; delete it when you fix it.\n- **Where Caliper's types differ from RDT and the checker, and what that costs** → `rdt-differences.md`.\n- **What broke and why, historically** → `rdt-coverage.md` — every bug found during real-library validation, root cause, and the fix. Keep this updated; it's the project's memory.\n- **Why a hard-to-reverse decision was made** → `docs/adr/` — OXC over the TypeScript compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack encoding, panic containment, the TypeScript 7 semantic backend. Write a new one when you make a \n- **How the pipeline fits together** → `ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `docs/architecture/` for per-subsystem invariants and known gaps (moved from `.claude/semantic-model/` so every coding agent can read it, not just Claude Code — `AGENTS.md` is no\n- **Setup, testing, code style, commit conventions** → `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n- **Migrating from react-docgen-typescript** → `MIGRATING.md`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"3455c280-cd2e-4079-95bf-76919eec302f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf6-483","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxViolations":[],"sandboxed":true,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"79952ce0-ef07-4aac-92a5-4f51f2589a10","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf6-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
