{"parentUuid":"40407497-25c6-4fda-b669-4cdbe5e96fbe","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"08d8dfa9-12ad-4625-aa58-11e91c631e1d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Ys9ocEHQ5ykjKiw9kCmKy","type":"tool_result","content":"# Storybook parity\n\nWhat the Storybook addon adds to, and costs against, Storybook's own docgen on real repositories: how often the addon hands a component on, what it documents that Storybook doesn't, where the two disagree, and what each costs. The numbers b\n\n## What is compared\n\n| Side | How it runs |\n| --- | --- |\n| Storybook's docgen | `@storybook/react`'s own `docgen-worker.js` (react-component-meta), unmodified, called as a middleware. It needs the TypeScript 5/6 compiler API, so `typescript` is redirected to `apps/oracle`'s TypeScript 6; this pac\n| The addon | `dist/provider.js`, the real `createDocgenProvider`, with Storybook's `meta.component` resolver and argTypes converter. |\n\nVariants of the addon:\n\n| Variant                | `loadDependencies` | `collapseInheritedProps` | `fallback`                           |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------ |\n| `caliper`              | on                 | none                     | degraded (the addon's defaults)      |\n| `caliper-nodeps`       | off                | none                     | degraded (what the addon did before) |\n| `caliper-curated`      | on                 | dependencies             | degraded                             |\n| `caliper-never`        | on                 | none                     | never                                |\n| `caliper-nodeps-never` | off                | none                     | never                                |\n\nThe `-never` variants answer for every component whatever its diagnostics say. Comparing them shows the information the addon holds; comparing the others shows what the `degraded` rule lets through.\n\nTwo story sets per corpus:\n\n- **Real stories**: the corpus's own `*.stories.*` files that name `component:` (Chakra: 1 of 125, Spectrum: 129 of 132; Mantine, shadcn and antd have none).\n- **Sampled components**: one generated `export default { component }` story per sampled component (`--sample`), written beside the component and removed afterwards. Components that aren't a named export, or the file's own default export un\n\nPer story, both sides' argTypes are reduced to control kind (`type.name`), options, required, type text, default and whether a description exists, then diffed prop by prop. **Extra props** are props only the addon lists. The report also has\n\nThe report sorts every disagreement in a table of **deliberate** differences and ones **for review**:\n\n- Deliberate: extra props that are DOM, React or ARIA attributes (the addon's `htmlAttributes: 'full'` default, `packages/storybook/src/options.ts`; `HtmlAttributeMode` in `crates/core/src/types/options.rs`), extra props inherited from a li\n- For review: props Storybook lists that aren't DOM attributes, type text that differs beyond formatting, `required` differing, and defaults only Storybook has. Each is listed by story and prop in the Markdown (the first 12) and in full in \n\nThe classes are heuristics: a DOM-attribute pattern, and a formatting-only normaliser that doesn't understand every TypeScript printer difference, so the review lists include differences that read the same to a person.\n\nNot measured: Storybook's control inference from argTypes (kind is `type.name`), and runtime behaviour in a real Storybook process (the worker thread, concurrency, caching). Timings include the first request, which starts the session; the T\n\n## Results\n\n### 2026-11-06, main at `c5fbb33e`: should an opaque prop hand the component on?\n\nThe `degraded` rule counts warnings and errors. A prop the extractor cannot expand (`keyof typeof x`, `-1 | 0`, an indexed access, a mapped or conditional type) is an `info` diagnostic (`OPAQUE_TYPE`, `INDEXED_ACCESS_OPAQUE`) and does not h\n\nComponents the addon would hand on, today (warning or error) and with the rule extended to `info` `OPAQUE_TYPE` or `INDEXED_ACCESS_OPAQUE`:\n\n| Corpus  | Components | Handed on today | Also handed on if opaque counts | Total |\n| ------- | ---------- | --------------- | ------------------------------- | ----- |\n| Mantine | 351        | 30 (8.5%)       | 262 (74.6%)                     | 83.2% |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7b38397a-d17c-415c-bb92-9e7491fa4e43","timestamp":"2026-11-16T06:35:10.669Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Storybook parity\n\nWhat the Storybook addon adds to, and costs against, Storybook's own docgen on real repositories: how often the addon hands a component on, what it documents that Storybook doesn't, where the two disagree, and what each costs. The numbers b\n\n## What is compared\n\n| Side | How it runs |\n| --- | --- |\n| Storybook's docgen | `@storybook/react`'s own `docgen-worker.js` (react-component-meta), unmodified, called as a middleware. It needs the TypeScript 5/6 compiler API, so `typescript` is redirected to `apps/oracle`'s TypeScript 6; this pac\n| The addon | `dist/provider.js`, the real `createDocgenProvider`, with Storybook's `meta.component` resolver and argTypes converter. |\n\nVariants of the addon:\n\n| Variant                | `loadDependencies` | `collapseInheritedProps` | `fallback`                           |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------ |\n| `caliper`              | on                 | none                     | degraded (the addon's defaults)      |\n| `caliper-nodeps`       | off                | none                     | degraded (what the addon did before) |\n| `caliper-curated`      | on                 | dependencies             | degraded                             |\n| `caliper-never`        | on                 | none                     | never                                |\n| `caliper-nodeps-never` | off                | none                     | never                                |\n\nThe `-never` variants answer for every component whatever its diagnostics say. Comparing them shows the information the addon holds; comparing the others shows what the `degraded` rule lets through.\n\nTwo story sets per corpus:\n\n- **Real stories**: the corpus's own `*.stories.*` files that name `component:` (Chakra: 1 of 125, Spectrum: 129 of 132; Mantine, shadcn and antd have none).\n- **Sampled components**: one generated `export default { component }` story per sampled component (`--sample`), written beside the component and removed afterwards. Components that aren't a named export, or the file's own default export un\n\nPer story, both sides' argTypes are reduced to control kind (`type.name`), options, required, type text, default and whether a description exists, then diffed prop by prop. **Extra props** are props only the addon lists. The report also has\n\nThe report sorts every disagreement in a table of **deliberate** differences and ones **for review**:\n\n- Deliberate: extra props that are DOM, React or ARIA attributes (the addon's `htmlAttributes: 'full'` default, `packages/storybook/src/options.ts`; `HtmlAttributeMode` in `crates/core/src/types/options.rs`), extra props inherited from a li\n- For review: props Storybook lists that aren't DOM attributes, type text that differs beyond formatting, `required` differing, and defaults only Storybook has. Each is listed by story and prop in the Markdown (the first 12) and in full in \n\nThe classes are heuristics: a DOM-attribute pattern, and a formatting-only normaliser that doesn't understand every TypeScript printer difference, so the review lists include differences that read the same to a person.\n\nNot measured: Storybook's control inference from argTypes (kind is `type.name`), and runtime behaviour in a real Storybook process (the worker thread, concurrency, caching). Timings include the first request, which starts the session; the T\n\n## Results\n\n### 2026-11-06, main at `c5fbb33e`: should an opaque prop hand the component on?\n\nThe `degraded` rule counts warnings and errors. A prop the extractor cannot expand (`keyof typeof x`, `-1 | 0`, an indexed access, a mapped or conditional type) is an `info` diagnostic (`OPAQUE_TYPE`, `INDEXED_ACCESS_OPAQUE`) and does not h\n\nComponents the addon would hand on, today (warning or error) and with the rule extended to `info` `OPAQUE_TYPE` or `INDEXED_ACCESS_OPAQUE`:\n\n| Corpus  | Components | Handed on today | Also handed on if opaque counts | Total |\n| ------- | ---------- | --------------- | ------------------------------- | ----- |\n| Mantine | 351        | 30 (8.5%)       | 262 (74.6%)                     | 83.2% |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"3455c280-cd2e-4079-95bf-76919eec302f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf6-483","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxViolations":[],"sandboxed":true,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"40407497-25c6-4fda-b669-4cdbe5e96fbe","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","session