{"parentUuid":"802fd3dc-944f-4689-9c02-b0d0945b0753","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5b05b98d-d44f-4d67-93b5-bcbfb7aafe7f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W6AoRTxyB6nW5y9ztMovAJ","type":"tool_result","content":"21:The workflow runs on every push to `main`, daily at 05:23 UTC, and on manual dispatch. Every run first asks `callisto release pending` for the oldest merged release commit whose tags or GitHub Release are missing, and finishes that one before anything newer\n48:## Recover a failed release\n55:callisto release pending --from 2daef9276b234fcc04d8994d91210eeccd88d7e8\n58:`--from` is the `RELEASE_PENDING_FROM` value in `callisto-release.yml`. Without it, `release pending` reads the committed decision of the 10 newest release commits and stops with E166 on one whose decision no longer decodes. The pin is the 0.9.0 release com\n60:0.9.0 was published before GitHub Releases were enabled, so `release pending` lists it as missing its GitHub Release. The first run after this flow lands finishes it: the build matrix rebuilds 0.9.0 from its release commit and Callisto creates the GitHub Re\n63:- **A release cannot finish:** dispatch it by hand with its release commit, `gh workflow run callisto-release.yml --ref main -f release_source_sha=<merged release commit>`. If it will never finish, skip it by moving `RELEASE_PENDING_FROM` to a newer release\n72:- **E180, the workflow cannot push a tag:** GitHub rejects a `GITHUB_TOKEN` tag push when the tagged commit's workflows differ from every branch tip, which happens when recovering an older release. Push each tag of that release yourself with a personal toke\n73:- **E140, attestation verification failed:** `gh attestation verify` rejected an asset: wrong repository, signer workflow, signer digest, source digest, or a self-hosted runner. The signer digest is the commit that ran `plan` (`--orchestration-revision`), s","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1ee45be2-a439-4696-9f3b-b7f230839dcc",