{"parentUuid":"3a543886-ad21-4de3-8ec8-2baaac34495c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch6Bu2R2PaBYCNbkZYzP9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RzQ3DcGZCSPTrQj4PDHX4t","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Alpha docs: addon upgrade note and known limits","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Write the alpha-facing documentation for caliper's Storybook addon, from `origin/main` (`git fetch origin` first; if blocked use existing refs), local branch `docs/alpha-limits-and-upgrade`; commit locally; I push. Read /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md, AGENTS.md ('Writing and commits': succinct, no banned words listed in docs/adr/README.md, never hard-wrap Markdown), README.md, MIGRATING.md, packages/storybook/README.md, docs/edge-cases.md, docs/STATUS.md (only its 'Known gaps' parts; do NOT touch its speed numbers: they are refreshed after the oracle run). Task, three small edits: (1) MIGRATING.md: a section 'Upgrading the Storybook addon' explaining the `collapseInheritedProps` default change from 'none' to 'dependencies' (what changes in Controls: a source of more than 200 props, or an ambient DOM/ARIA/style source of more than 30, becomes one inheritance layer of names with no Controls row per prop; own props and notable inherited props (onClick, onFocus, onBlur, className, style, id, tabIndex, aria-label) stay listed; a story arg naming a collapsed prop shows as undocumented), the one-line opt-out (`collapseInheritedProps: 'none'`), and the other values ('all'); check the real option names/values in packages/storybook/src/options.ts and crates/core/src/types/options.rs and quote them exactly. (2) packages/storybook/README.md (and the root README only if it has an addon section): a short 'Known limits (alpha)' list, each limit one bullet a user will hit, verified against the code/docs, no invented ones. Candidates to veri