{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","id":"760b4ded-03ca-471b-83e3-b495b2b00b87","timestamp":"2026-11-16T07:10:43.326Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"9803daf85cbe48be5f6ca225f95dc13bf2e5a024e85e5325762dd209c1ad3e02","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"8024409a-5c74-4ef9-82f9-6e68cd0b7de3","keep":1295,"tail":["a589b9dbeabe20d8f53cfa2fefe45ef567816c9131069fc029fd214737cb150b","53dfb2cf34e802960217ed3a6e2113b5507211020b59ae144b0c547f2352a930","9e672f737c8f0cb9ef2d69d7b889f682a5168366108db95c1e4e82ba37be477e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1297,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"c7453926946b197da505f636d5c4fff4b51d525b7e82bd8cd2d7a6ff206966a8"}
{"parentUuid":"f5ab0bbf-9904-4a49-8588-25876ca9f751","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch6BwHJnXLur8tEi56yhP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The oracle's CLI half is mostly in. Storybook dev mode and the Spectrum corpus are still running, and the timings are provisional because the machine wasn't quiet.\n\n**Caveat on timings.** Load averages were 6.7–8.6 (and 12.7 over fifteen minutes at the start). The harness waited 900 seconds for quiet, then ran anyway. Every wall time below is inflated by contention, so read them as upper bounds. Memory and output size aren't affected.\n\n**CLI, checker on, `--runs 2`** (first run is cold, second keeps the cache):\n\n| Corpus | First run | Peak RSS | Second run | react-docgen-typescript (RDT) | Faster than RDT | JSON |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Chakra | 3.5 s | 1,876 MiB | 0.76 s | 22.5 s, 2,847 MiB | 6.4× | 47 MB |\n| Mantine | 1.07 s | 853 MiB | 0.27 s | 1.50 s, 549 MiB | 1.4× | 55 MB |\n| shadcn | 1.43 s | 954 MiB | 0.43 s | 3.83 s, 1,593 MiB | 2.7× | 5.3 MB |\n| antd | 1.45 s | 1,060 MiB | 0.09 s | 2.21 s, 1,056 MiB | 1.5× | 4.4 MB |\n| Spectrum | 1.9 s | not yet read | 0.5 s | not yet read | not yet read | not yet read |\n\nNo run failed. Chakra is the one that used to take 42 GB on 0.11.0. Now it uses 1.9 GiB and finishes in 3.5 s.\n\n**Quality (the oracle's check of prop types against the TypeScript checker):**\n\n| Corpus | Props | Correct | Wrong | Less precise | Not judged |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| shadcn | 13,932 | 13,748 | 0 | 37 | 93 |\n| antd | 4,127 | 3,838 | 1 | 86 | 202 |\n| Mantine | 20,148 | 6,589 | 0 | 870 | 12,681 |\n\nMantine has a lot of \"not judged\" props, so its right-rate means little until I know why. Chakra has no headline row yet, which may be a failed oracle step. The worker will say.\n\n**Recall against RDT:** Chakra 614 of 664 components, with 485,975 of 485,975 of its own props. Mantine 328 of 368, shadcn 1,527 of 1,573, antd 188 of 202.\n\n**Still running:** the first-versus-second-run script, Chakra's headline, Storybook dev mode (cold start, time to structural Controls, the checker's upgrade, neighbour navigation, edit time and memory), and the 0.11.0 comparison. The final report goes to `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md`.\n\n**What I'd do about the load.** Another agent's build was running on this machine during the weekly. Once the worker finishes, I'd re-time the first and second runs on an idle machine and use those numbers as the official ones.\n\n**Release pipeline (separate).** The \"Execute approved release\" failure is the unfinished 0.11.0 release hitting E167 on every `main` push. The docs give the recovery: delete the mismatched asset and re-dispatch, or move `RELEASE_PENDING_FROM` past it to skip it. Both touch the real release or its assets, so I won't do either without your say-so. Which do you want?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1086,"cache_read_input_tokens":752228,"output_tokens":1203,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1086,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1203,"cache_read_input_tokens":752228,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1086,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1086},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6fec3267-6930-470a-8860-44640b643456","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch6BwGzReg2DvrDeHYJUT","requestRef":"760b4ded-03ca-471b-83e3-b495b2b00b87","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d882cce3-1d84-4685-8a46