{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","id":"7c287645-bd97-4515-a1d2-441fb3c04059","timestamp":"2026-11-16T07:38:43.458Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"9803daf85cbe48be5f6ca225f95dc13bf2e5a024e85e5325762dd209c1ad3e02","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"87269375-740c-406f-8842-a42414730a8e","keep":1323,"tail":["959f630b66b2a85700c202e6bc18a3c8b8408aa6bca996922f97e3084d99f94e","e741739fff2b80ed53caaf6f8579c7dd2835839133a44c4a9815e402adf64c9d","52ae2a0e30a854ecb707bb5d23052d5f85ecd32f964518b111d2cd9ab3a40385"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1325,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"be879436cd68db6273deccde4959a416a693d4c36521af13c52ff36ea1849b62"}
{"parentUuid":"8ab9ed08-9df4-4502-9b67-ff94643a405a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch6E58ZdgAsfHrz48MWMR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Performance is solid on current `main`. Output quality has two open problems, and a diagnosis is running. The full report is at `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md`.\n\nAll timings were taken at machine load 5–10, so wall times are inflated. Memory and sizes are unaffected.\n\n**Performance (checker on, the default)**\n\n| Corpus | First run | Second run | vs react-docgen-typescript (RDT) | Budget |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Chakra | 3.5 s, 1.9 GiB | 0.77 s, 476 MiB | 6.4× / 29× faster | pass |\n| Mantine | 1.06 s, 857 MiB | 0.27 s | 1.4× / 5.6× | pass |\n| antd | 1.49 s, 1.07 GiB | 0.08 s | 1.5× / 28× | pass |\n| shadcn | 1.41 s, 981 MiB | 0.42 s | 2.7× / 9× | pass |\n| Spectrum | 1.56 s, 840 MiB | 0.23 s | 1.4× / 9.6× | pass |\n\n- **The 0.11.0 problem is gone.** Chakra went from 42 GB (6.9 GB with the fix) to 1.9 GiB.\n- **Structural-only floor:** 0.07–0.49 s.\n\n**Storybook dev mode (real browser, Chakra `Button`)**\n- **Cold:** structural Controls arrive 891 ms after the story renders, and the checker's answer replaces them 134 ms later.\n- **Warm:** Controls arrive 128–156 ms after render, already the checker's answer.\n- **Live edit:** a new prop shows up 172 ms after the file write.\n- **Memory:** 893 MiB.\n- **Not measured:** prefetch of neighbouring stories, and antd, whose generated `./version` import fails in Vite.\n\n**Quality problems**\n1. **`Button` shows 437 Controls rows, not about 146.**\n   - About 300 are `@types/react` DOM, ARIA and event props, and about 130 are Chakra condition props such as `_active` and `2xl`.\n   - A plain `ComponentProps<'span'>` component shows 280 rows.\n   - The 705-name `SystemProperties` layer does collapse correctly.\n   - This is the exact noise collapse was meant to remove, so it's the top alpha issue.\n2. **`@types/react` props are almost absent with the checker on.**\n   - Recall against RDT: Mantine 0.4%, Chakra about 0%, shadcn 4.9%, antd 24%. 0.10.0 without the checker was above 99%.\n   - It may be intended (the checker lane lets the element layer stand for those props). It may also be tied to why the Storybook rows stay high.\n3. **The oracle can't run Chakra on Node's default heap.** It ran out of memory, so Chakra has no right-rate.\n4. **Mantine's right-rate is 32.7%** because 62.9% of its props are \"not judged\", with 0 wrong.\n\nThe right-rates elsewhere are good: shadcn 98.7%, antd 93.0%, Spectrum 88.4%.\n\n**Diagnosis running.** An Opus worker (50 calls, no fixes) will check whether (1) and (2) are intended or regressions. It starts by checking whether the Storybook demo pins `collapseInheritedProps: 'none'` from the earlier harness. It names the cause with file and line, the commit if it's a regression, and the smallest fix. It writes to `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/diagnosis.md`.\n\n**Caveats**\n- The worker never got a quiet machine. I'd re-time once nothing else is building.\n- No real 0.11.0 weekly record exists to compare against: the CI weekly died on Chakra with exit 143.\n\nFor the alpha, I'd treat (1) as a blocker, since it shows the user the noise we set out to remove. I'd treat (3) as a fix to the weekly workflow (the Node heap). (4) needs a look at what \"not judged\" means for Mantine's types."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5283,"cache_read_input_tokens":780322,"output_tokens":1392,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5283,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1392,"cache_read_input_tokens":780322,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5283,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5283},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"bdc68d1a-11de-4008-ad22-61cd93831b8d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch6E58FX7QjeTUjPGc9kz","requestRef":"7c287645-bd97-4515-a1d2-441fb3c04059","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"aec97730-4385-48a6-a158-1c3826dd0b6b","timestamp":"2026-11-16T07:38:52.583Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf6-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
