{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","prNumber":489,"prUrl":"https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/489","prRepository":"orin-dx/caliper","timestamp":"2026-11-16T07:43:29.269Z"}
{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytvK9B32ZaSUaSe6aAZ","lastSequenceNum":15975,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"9e3da8bb-30a0-4683-bcb8-f4d3969ff3f7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch6ESCQteUMgV1KgMrpDh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Neither problem is a regression: both were already in 0.11.0, and both are documented behavior. They do show a real contract gap for the alpha. The diagnosis is in `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/diagnosis.md`.\n\n**A. Why Storybook shows 437 rows for `Button`**\n- **Cause:** the addon defaults to `htmlAttributes: 'full'`, which lists all of `@types/react`'s real attributes, about 290 for a button. Collapse exempts `@types/react` by design, so the DOM props never collapse.\n- **The other 130:** these are Chakra's `Conditions` props (`_active`, `2xl`, …). They are under the 200-prop threshold and aren't recognized as ambient by name.\n- **Why the earlier \"146\":** that was Chakra's own props plus the layer in the CLI's checker output. It never counted DOM props.\n- **Already there in 0.11.0.** The old demo showed 1,141 rows and collapse took it to 437.\n\n**B. `@types/react` props missing from the CLI output with the checker on**\n- **Cause:** since commit d072b2ed (0.8.0 through 0.11.0), the whole-project merge drops React's props whenever a component has an element layer, on the grounds that the layer \"stands for them\".\n- **The catch:** that layer carries no member names, so a CLI or RDT-format consumer gets no DOM prop names at all, and `htmlAttributes: 'full'` doesn't bring them back.\n- **Who it affects:** not Storybook, which goes through the session lane. It affects CLI users and the weekly's recall metric.\n- **It surfaced now** only because 0.11.0 turned the checker on by default.\n\nThe two lanes disagree on the same options: the CLI checker lane shows `Button` with 150 props and `Badge` with 2, while Storybook shows 437 and 280.\n\n**Options, from the diagnosis**\n1. **Config only:** default the addon to `htmlAttributes: 'curated'`. `Button` goes to 314 rows and `Badge` to 161, which still isn't the expected shape.\n2. **Contract fix (recommended):** when collapse is on, treat `@types/react`'s element attributes as the ambient layer they already are. List only the 17 notable ones for `button` (`onClick`, `className`, and so on) and leave the rest to the layer. `Button` would show about 167 rows and `Badge` about 2 plus its notables. It touches about four Rust files and needs a model test. Both lanes then agree, which also settles B.\n3. **Optional on top:** recognize Chakra's `Conditions` as ambient. `Button` drops to about 37 rows.\n4. **For B alone:** either change the weekly to count React props as recalled when the element layer exists (one file, no output change), or make the CLI merge honor `htmlAttributes` like the session lane does (restores about 99% recall).\n\n**My recommendation for the alpha:** do option 2, so both lanes agree and Controls show the roughly 20 real props. Treat option 3 as a follow-up. For the weekly, fix the recall metric so it stops measuring a removed feature.\n\nOption 2 changes what Storybook users see by default and moves a documented contract, so I want your go-ahead. Shall I plan it as one slice, with an oracle check that `Button` lands at about 167 rows and recall stays correct?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7373,"cache_read_input_tokens":787628,"output_tokens":1126,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7373,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1126,"cache_read_input_tokens":787628,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7373,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7373},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6d9affd4-d9ce-482f-9dde-00e32fad11cd","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch6ESC2KQwynacttTynyx","requestRef":"6e286b4f-6c9d-4d91-b01f-6235d7eacdee","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"391e5940-e264-4293-b1e6-190d88a2e15a","timestamp":"2026-11-16T07:43:37.644Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf6-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
