{"attachment":{"command":"","content":"","durationMs":45,"exitCode":0,"hookEvent":"","hookName":"","stderr":"","stdout":"","toolUseID":"","type":"hook_success"},"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"mf-t4","isSidechain":false,"parentUuid":"c6a9da1e-8ba0-4943-acea-d29f2cc4871c","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano","timestamp":"2026-11-16T17:33:51.723Z","type":"attachment","userType":"external","uuid":"9bfc597e-a672-4a98-bb2a-964eea40c3c5","version":"2.1.311"}
{"parentUuid":"6b949900-be6d-4134-a5f6-16e4d931e9be","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"21c5cb8b-2147-40ac-910c-28fb083963c8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E8Hk4d2F2St2wLsDom3odN","type":"tool_result","content":"## What\n\nSlice T4 of ADR 0028 (trail 405). The rows a user sees (`props` and `notableInherited`, which Storybook turns into Controls and the RDT view into props) now follow the placement relevance's `decide` computes. Both lanes go through one sink.\n\n- **One placement.** `relevance::apply` keeps `decide`'s placement on the entry (`ComponentEntry::relevance`, not serialized) and lists by it (`relevance::narrow`). Both checker merges (the session's and the CLI's `apply_props`) call `narrow` again. Both take a `@types/react` prop only where the structural answer lists it (`reac\n- **Provenance, not names.** A placed member is kept with the source the structural answer gives it. A listed prop leaves the listing only when its name and its `parent` both match. It then becomes a name in its source's layer: that layer, else the element layer for an ambient source, else a new layer of that parent.\n  - A prop with no known source stays listed, in both lanes.\n  - A same-named prop from another source is never hidden.\n  - A homomorphic mapped type's member (`{ [K in keyof Conditions]?: V }`) now keeps its key's interface as `parent`, as the checker does. Without this, Chakra's condition props had a source in only one lane.\n- **Scope.** Only sources outside the project are narrowed: a dependency's, React's or the DOM's, decided by declaring path. Project sources keep the collapse rule. `collapseInheritedProps: none` narrows nothing: it is the expanded view (`relevance: 'all'`).\n- **`decide`.**\n  - A member passed at the call-site floor is a typed row even if it is ambient.\n  - An ambient member the body only reads is a `used` name.\n  - An ambient member with unknown evidence is a layer name.\n  - A member put forward that has no typed row is named in `used`.\n  - With no evidence at all, the listing is own, picked, overriding, required and defaulted props. A whole DOM source is never listed.\n- **Declined key sets.** A `Pick` or `Omit` (in place or behind an alias) whose keys are not a closed set of string literals narrows no non-ambient source (D5). React's and the DOM's attributes are still narrowed. Keys a `Pick` names through `Omit`, `Partial`, `Required`, `Readonly` or a project alias count as picked.\n- **JSX children** now pass `children` at a call site, after every attribute, as the JSX transform does. Parse cache schema 44.\n- **`htmlAttributes`** still defaults to `full`. It now says which attributes are known, not which are rows: an attribute can become a typed row only if it is known, and `curated` leaves most unknown. `notable_html_attrs` now only feeds `curated`; R9 deletes it.\n- ADR 0028 is amended (section A2). ADR 0023 is cited by `options.rs` but is not in `docs/adr`, so A2 records its contract change. Changeset `list-props-by-usage` (minor). The output schema is unchanged (8).\n\nInvoked invariants:\n- Unknown unless proven: no source means listed; a declined key set narrows no non-ambient source; only ambient unknowns go to layers.\n- Resolved by binding: provenance is (name, type, file), never a name alone.\n- Every read recorded: the delta rule `layers_differ` now compares the listing too.\n- One owner: `decide` decides once, `narrow` enforces the decision.\n- Wired or not defined: `used` is produced by body reads and by passed members of collapsed sources.\n\n## Evidence\n\nStorybook dev mode (sb-demo, this branch's addon and napi, cold cache):\n\n- Button: 437 rows before, 10 after. The 10 are `children` (Storybook adds it from the story's args), extra, fresh, kind, loading, recipe, size, spinnerPlacement, tone, variant.\n- Badge: 280 rows before, 3 after: `children` (from the story's args), asChild, variant.\n\nThese were measured at 3bb819e3. At the final head, the CLI gives the same names in both lanes.\n\nCLI `extract` on sb-demo/src:\n\n- Checker lane: Button 150 → 9, Badge 2 → 2.\n- Structural lane (`--no-checker`): Button 439 → 9, Badge 281 → 2.\n- The 286 button and 279 span attributes are now names in the element layer. That layer had 0 members before.\n\nOwn-props differential, main vs this branch. It lists the names listed before but not after, among props whose `parent` file is outside `node_modules` (or that have no parent):\n\n- Chakra, Mantine and antd: empty.\n- sb-demo: empty.\n- shadcn: 10 components lose `children` (`Command*` over cmdk). The structural answer declares it in `@types/react`'s `DOMAttributes`; the checker reported it with no parent. These components have fewer than 3 call sites, so it is a layer name. This is not a project-declared prop.\n- Spectrum: 972 components lose `aria-*`, `id` and similar props. They are declared in `@react-types/shared/src/dom.d.ts`, which ADR 0028 classes as ambient by path (`Origin::SharedDom`). It is a project file, but it holds the DOM's attributes, so the rule treats it like `@types/react`. If the owner wants SharedDom kept listed, \n\nButton rows per corpus:\n\n- Chakra's own `Button`: 146 → 147 (project sources are not narrowed; `children` is now passed).\n- antd `Button`: 23 → 25.\n- shadcn new-york `Button`: 4 → 4.\n- shadcn aria `Button`: 51 → 40.\n- Spectrum `Button`: 83 → 77.\n- react-aria-components `Button`: 113 → 38.\n\nFive corpora, main de016f69 vs ce276f1a (checker on, `--load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies`, one run each, load 16 to 31):","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"382798d1-53fc-4fba-bbdb-e0bf0ab2e411","timestamp":"2026-11-16T17:33:55.303Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## What\n\nSlice T4 of ADR 0028 (trail 405). The rows a user sees (`props` and `notableInherited`, which Storybook turns into Controls and the RDT view into props) now follow the placement relevance's `decide` computes. Both lanes go through one sink.\n\n- **One placement.** `relevance::apply` keeps `decide`'s placement on the entry (`ComponentEntry::relevance`, not serialized) and lists by it (`relevance::narrow`). Both checker merges (the session's and the CLI's `apply_props`) call `narrow` again. Both take a `@types/react` prop only where the structural answer lists it (`reac\n- **Provenance, not names.** A placed member is kept with the source the structural answer gives it. A listed prop leaves the listing only when its name and its `parent` both match. It then becomes a name in its source's layer: that layer, else the element layer for an ambient source, else a new layer of that parent.\n  - A prop with no known source stays listed, in both lanes.\n  - A same-named prop from another source is never hidden.\n  - A homomorphic mapped type's member (`{ [K in keyof Conditions]?: V }`) now keeps its key's interface as `parent`, as the checker does. Without this, Chakra's condition props had a source in only one lane.\n- **Scope.** Only sources outside the project are narrowed: a dependency's, React's or the DOM's, decided by declaring path. Project sources keep the collapse rule. `collapseInheritedProps: none` narrows nothing: it is the expanded view (`relevance: 'all'`).\n- **`decide`.**\n  - A member passed at the call-site floor is a typed row even if it is ambient.\n  - An ambient member the body only reads is a `used` name.\n  - An ambient member with unknown evidence is a layer name.\n  - A member put forward that has no typed row is named in `used`.\n  - With no evidence at all, the listing is own, picked, overriding, required and defaulted props. A whole DOM source is never listed.\n- **Declined key sets.** A `Pick` or `Omit` (in place or behind an alias) whose keys are not a closed set of string literals narrows no non-ambient source (D5). React's and the DOM's attributes are still narrowed. Keys a `Pick` names through `Omit`, `Partial`, `Required`, `Readonly` or a project alias count as picked.\n- **JSX children** now pass `children` at a call site, after every attribute, as the JSX transform does. Parse cache schema 44.\n- **`htmlAttributes`** still defaults to `full`. It now says which attributes are known, not which are rows: an attribute can become a typed row only if it is known, and `curated` leaves most unknown. `notable_html_attrs` now only feeds `curated`; R9 deletes it.\n- ADR 0028 is amended (section A2). ADR 0023 is cited by `options.rs` but is not in `docs/adr`, so A2 records its contract change. Changeset `list-props-by-usage` (minor). The output schema is unchanged (8).\n\nInvoked invariants:\n- Unknown unless proven: no source means listed; a declined key set narrows no non-ambient source; only ambient unknowns go to layers.\n- Resolved by binding: provenance is (name, type, file), never a name alone.\n- Every read recorded: the delta rule `layers_differ` now compares the listing too.\n- One owner: `decide` decides once, `narrow` enforces the decision.\n- Wired or not defined: `used` is produced by body reads and by passed members of collapsed sources.\n\n## Evidence\n\nStorybook dev mode (sb-demo, this branch's addon and napi, cold cache):\n\n- Button: 437 rows before, 10 after. The 10 are `children` (Storybook adds it from the story's args), extra, fresh, kind, loading, recipe, size, spinnerPlacement, tone, variant.\n- Badge: 280 rows before, 3 after: `children` (from the story's args), asChild, variant.\n\nThese were measured at 3bb819e3. At the final head, the CLI gives the same names in both lanes.\n\nCLI `extract` on sb-demo/src:\n\n- Checker lane: Button 150 → 9, Badge 2 → 2.\n- Structural lane (`--no-checker`): Button 439 → 9, Badge 281 → 2.\n- The 286 button and 279 span attributes are now names in the element layer. That layer had 0 members before.\n\nOwn-props differential, main vs this branch. It lists the names listed before but not after, among props whose `parent` file is outside `node_modules` (or that have no parent):\n\n- Chakra, Mantine and antd: empty.\n- sb-demo: empty.\n- shadcn: 10 components lose `children` (`Command*` over cmdk). The structural answer declares it in `@types/react`'s `DOMAttributes`; the checker reported it with no parent. These components have fewer than 3 call sites, so it is a layer name. This is not a project-declared prop.\n- Spectrum: 972 components lose `aria-*`, `id` and similar props. They are declared in `@react-types/shared/src/dom.d.ts`, which ADR 0028 classes as ambient by path (`Origin::SharedDom`). It is a project file, but it holds the DOM's attributes, so the rule treats it like `@types/react`. If the owner wants SharedDom kept listed, \n\nButton rows per corpus:\n\n- Chakra's own `Button`: 146 → 147 (project sources are not narrowed; `children` is now passed).\n- antd `Button`: 23 → 25.\n- shadcn new-york `Button`: 4 → 4.\n- shadcn aria `Button`: 51 → 40.\n- Spectrum `Button`: 83 → 77.\n- react-aria-components `Button`: 113 → 38.\n\nFive corpora, main de016f69 vs ce276f1a (checker on, `--load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies`, one run each, load 16 to 31):","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f3eda9f1-0a08-46cb-bfc9-1c9870e55b8b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf-t4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/w