{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","id":"e76554b5-afc7-491e-902b-6627a7322620","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:08:02.439Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"9803daf85cbe48be5f6ca225f95dc13bf2e5a024e85e5325762dd209c1ad3e02","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"fd9f0481-2e43-4139-abc9-f42d235b6fa1","keep":1392,"tail":["cf5ca3811b4347f362de7b67ff739cd9c5ea888addcfd75e3f28473b301f7059","8e64a8e6a2d94a8cf028856c3f8bdd6fad7f2753622823b4da9f71efe1d09eb8","9e672f737c8f0cb9ef2d69d7b889f682a5168366108db95c1e4e82ba37be477e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1394,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"89a187dfb317f7d5366370ebcde64437d484df6256e87ea8f6e7d80756e2dd90"}
{"parentUuid":"bb7f95c3-5caa-4d69-8ff1-e71fe2610eed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch744WVoazCxYpZMSCB7E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's where we stand: the code work is nearly done, and what's left is merging #490, a few decisions, and release plumbing.\n\n**Done and merged**\n- Everything from the collapse, relevance, scheduler and factory work is on `main`.\n- Changesets and docs: #488 is merged, and I merged #489 (the upgrade note and known limits) as far as I can tell. It's still open and blocked, waiting on you.\n\n**In review now: #490, listing props by usage**\n- **CI:** every check is green: lint, the full Rust suite, the checker lane, the construct suite, TypeScript on Node 24 and 26, SemVer, MSRV, Coverage, the Vite plugin and the install matrix. The corpora budget gate is skipped, because it only runs on a release PR.\n- **Effect:** Chakra `Button` goes from 437 Controls rows to 10, `Badge` from 280 to 3, and the CLI agrees with Storybook.\n- **Findings:** I haven't seen Entire findings on it yet.\n- **Waiting on you:** is hiding Spectrum's `aria-*` and `id` by default acceptable? I need your say-so before this merges.\n- **Open before I'd call it done:**\n  - shadcn first-run memory is +22% (986 → 1,204 MiB).\n  - 4 code-review items weren't fixed (`key` in the CLI, allocations in `narrow`, an unused parameter, a double alias walk).\n  - I haven't read the diff.\n\n**Release and alpha plumbing, all waiting on you**\n- **The 0.11.0 release recovery.** It fails on every `main` push with E167. The choice is to delete the mismatched asset and re-dispatch, or skip it with `RELEASE_PENDING_FROM`. Either one touches the real release, so I haven't done it.\n- **Your two other alpha decisions:** the audience, and whether the addon default flip ships in the first alpha. You confirmed the definition of the alpha itself.\n- **The \"add-on\" wording.** I haven't swept the docs yet, and I'd like to confirm what you meant by it.\n\n**Still to do**\n- **Weekly oracle:** needs the larger Node heap for Chakra and a way to report \"not judged\" separately, so Chakra's and Mantine's headline stops reading as 17% and 33%.\n- **Re-time on an idle machine.** The earlier numbers had load 5–10, and the T4 comparison ran at 16–31.\n- **After #490 merges:** refresh the `STATUS.md` numbers and re-run the oracle on that SHA.\n\n**Next steps, in order:** your answers on Spectrum and the release recovery, then #490's memory check and review items, then merge it. Then the weekly fix and one clean re-run on the merged `main`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_read_input_tokens":833680,"output_tokens":922,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1242,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":922,"cache_read_input_tokens":833680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1242},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"04781197-9825-403e-8e24-4d1e199584e4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch744W9UNmZ9PrQHn9Ct2","requestRef":"e76554b5-afc7-491e-902b-6627a7322620","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"84493687-464b-4af9-ab96-bb6486f67733","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:08:10.322Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983