{"parentUuid":"68cb0f37-1129-4720-835f-f526b339216b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch74CFoEToQZCLuhYRHvh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The memory profiling worker is running (60 calls, no changes, no push). I'll report its ranked list when it lands. The report will go to `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/memory-profile.md`.\n\nIt reports four things:\n1. **Peak RSS by phase** on Chakra, shadcn, Mantine and the demo: structural parse, dependency loading, checker program creation, per-component conversion, merge, and output.\n2. **What caused shadcn's +22% in #490.** The layer names went from 6,615 to 388,181 on shadcn. I suspect they're stored as owned strings, so interning them is a likely candidate.\n3. **Measured size of each saving:**\n   - Loading only the files each component reaches into the checker.\n   - Freeing phase data before the next phase.\n   - Streaming the output instead of building one 50 MB string.\n   - Interning layer names.\n   - Allocator settings.\n   - Any memory option tsrs exposes.\n4. **A top-three recommendation** with the expected Chakra peak, and a note on whether each helps the Storybook dev server (893 MiB) or only the one-shot CLI.\n\nEverything else is paused on #490's memory question, since the shadcn +22% is one of the first things this settles. Your Spectrum `aria-*` decision and the release recovery are still open."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7646,"cache_read_input_tokens":835923,"output_tokens":440,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7646,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":440,"cache_read_input_tokens":835923,"cac