{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytvK9B32ZaSUaSe6aAZ","lastSequenceNum":15975,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"7dbac199-3aa9-40f9-89e2-909e5c10c8b9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch75gwmwhuCdwegmAkPp9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both memory workers are running. Neither pushes. Each reports peak RSS before and after, an identity check, and its gate results.\n\n**Worker 1: #490's retained data** (Opus, 90 calls, on #490's branch)\n- **Target:** bring #490's peak back to within about 3% of `main`. That means shadcn at about 1,010 MiB or less (it's 1,195 now), Chakra at about 1,925 or less (it's 2,030), and shadcn's structural-only run at about 370 or less (it's 463).\n- **Output:** byte-identical to #490's head on all five corpora.\n- **Approach:** by measurement, smallest first. Stop keeping a placement object per component. Make components that name the same source layer share one list instead of each cloning its own. Then find what else grows in the component phase.\n- **If it must change `InheritedLayer`:** it's a public type, so it needs a semver-correct changeset, and the JSON must stay the same.\n\n**Worker 2: generic instantiation** (Opus, 90 calls, on `main`, so it's its own PR)\n- **Target:** remove the peak the profile found, where a second whole program is built while the first is alive. The bound is −262 MiB on Chakra, −231 on shadcn, −196 on Mantine.\n- **Output:** byte-identical to `main` on all five corpora and gate-large, and Storybook session answers for generic components must equal the batch ones.\n- **Options it tries, by measurement:** derive the program from the live snapshot, root it at only the generic components' files, or free the other lane's program and memo first.\n- **It also runs** the gate harness in determinism and memory modes, since it changes session code.\n\nBoth follow the pre-push gate: a mutation proof, then `/code-review medium` awaited with one fix round. When each reports, I'll check the identity and RSS results, push, and resolve any findings. The first lands on #490's branch, so #490 gets a memory fix before it merges.\n\n#3, sharing the converter's memo, is the larger job and the only route to Chakra under 1 GiB. I'll hold it until these two show what's left."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8770,"cache_read_input_tokens":859658,"output_tokens":692,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8770,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":692,"cache_read_input_tokens":859658,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8770,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8770},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c169d3cd-2603-429b-8738-68f835eb86d4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch75gwWa4KEFFJdoEsGFi","requestRef":"65cee227-5ef3-43e4-aac8-47cd23a9e553","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ee1c7c04-4d9c-4717-be06-97a1a3aee5f4","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:29:29.317Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
